Hawaii QSO Party -- the 14 Hawaii multiplier districts, each its own multiplier.
Three-letter codes from the sponsor's multiplier map (issue 118) and DXLog.net HIQP.txt (docs/ContestRules/QSOParties/Hawaii/HI-QSO-PARTY-Districts.txt).
No district maps to the state: every entrant counts each district as a multiplier of its own.
The districts are not ADIF counties, so the class writes no ADIF CNTY.
No INCLUDE here: an out-of-state entrant's table holds only the districts (the host-area rule reads it).
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

HIL = HIL,^Hilo
HON = HON,^Honolulu
KAL = KAL,^Kalawao
KAU = KAU,^Kauai
KOH = KOH,^Kohala
KON = KON,^Kona
LHN = LHN,^Leeward
LNI = LNI,^Lanai
MAU = MAU,^Maui
MOL = MOL,^Molokai
NII = NII,^Niihau
PRL = PRL,^Pearl Harbor Area
VOL = VOL,^Volcano Park
WHN = WHN,^Windward
